{
  "id": "ss.char.donut",
  "name": "Donut",
  "description": "The spine thrower: a rogue of the brood, hooded and masked. A dark red hood, a scarf drawn up over the nose, one brow raised over the eye that shows. The shell closed into a ring where the emitter chamber used to be, and Donut wears it as it is: a coral ring-plate over the chest with the hole open through it, the dead organ set on the rim off to one side, the way it always was. A dark leather jerkin under that, a bandolier of husk spines across the back rising over the far shoulder, a short red cloak, and in the near hand three wing blades fanned like a hand of cards: Drifter membranes on bone frames, thrown to bounce from body to body. The pouch on the belt is the jelly it hoards. The feelers rise from the hood and lie back along it. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
